📁 Repository Structure

The project is organized as follows:

VaaS/
│
├── prompts/
│   ├── zero_shot_1.yaml
│   ├── zero_shot_2.yaml
│   ├── zero_shot_3.yaml
│   ├── zero_shot_4.yaml
│   ├── few_shot_1.yaml
│   ├── few_shot_2.yaml
│   ├── few_shot_3.yaml
│   ├── few_shot_4.yaml
│   ├── cot_1.yaml
│   ├── cot_2.yaml
│   ├── cot_3.yaml
│   ├── cot_4.yaml
│
├── VaaS_Classification_Optimization.py
│   → Main script for running classification and optimization experiments
│
├── LLM_Evaluation.py
│   → Evaluation module for computing performance metrics
│     (Accuracy, Recall, F1-score, MCC, MAE, Composition Accuracy, AROL)
│
└── README.md
⚙️ Components Overview
1. Prompt Files (.yaml)

The repository includes 12 structured YAML prompt templates:

Zero-shot prompting (4 files)
Few-shot prompting (4 files)
Chain-of-Thought (CoT) prompting (4 files)

Each file defines the input format and instruction templates used to query LLMs.

2. Main Execution File
VaaS_Classification_Optimization.py

This is the main pipeline of the framework. It:

Loads datasets and prompt templates
Sends queries to LLMs
Executes classification and optimization tasks
Stores raw outputs for evaluation
3. Evaluation Module
LLM_Evaluation.py

This script is used to compute evaluation metrics, including:

Classification Accuracy
Recall
F1-score
Matthews Correlation Coefficient (MCC)
Mean Absolute Error (MAE)
Composition Accuracy
AROL (Average Relative Optimization Loss)
